== The crossing of the border: the family through the detector (standalone_SIM.py, learning mode) ==

-- 0. the detector of this script
   tracker: beam pipe r = 2.25 cm; pixel barrel r = 2.9, 6.8, 10.9, 16.0 cm; inner barrel 25.5 ... 49.8; outer barrel 60.8 ... 108.0;
            3 + 3 + 9 pairs of disks at |z| = 29 ... 266 cm; the boundary to the calorimeters at r = 123.3 cm, |z| = 293.5 cm
   ECAL: 61200 barrel crystals from r = 129 cm, |eta| < 1.479; 17376 endcap crystals at |z| = 320 cm, to |eta| = 3.0; preshower 1.653 < |eta| < 2.6
   HCAL: HB 9072 cells, HE 6768, HO 2160, HF 1728 (long and short fibres) at |z| = 1115 cm
   lead tungstate: X0 = 0.89 cm, Moliere radius 2.19 cm, critical energy 9.3 MeV, interaction length 20.3 cm; a crystal is 25.8 X0 and 1.13 lambda_I deep

-- 1. the magnetic field
   B = 3.8 T: R = pT / (0.3 B) = 87.8 cm x pT[GeV]; a track from the beam line reaches radius r only if pT > 0.3 B r / 2:
   pT > 0.735 GeV for the barrel ECAL (r = 129 cm), 0.702 for the edge of the tracker, 16.5 MeV for the first pixel layer
   307 of the 672 primaries are charged, 175 of them in |eta| < 2.5; 113 of those have pT < 0.735 GeV (median pT 0.55 GeV): they cannot reach the barrel ECAL
   in |eta| < 1.479: 107 charged, 65 of them loopers
   sensor crossings: 3419 on straight lines -> 3830 on helices; primaries at the boundary 672 -> 672
   the leading charged member of our jet: pi+ pT 14.27 GeV, eta -1.336: R = 12.5 m; over L = 1.1 m its sagitta is L^2 / 8R = 1.21 cm, its azimuth turns by asin(L / 2R) = 0.0439 rad

