-- 3. electromagnetic physics
   silicon: minimum of the Bethe-Bloch curve 1.666 MeV cm2/g at beta gamma = 3.5; a minimum-ionising particle loses on average 124 keV in 320 um, most probably 84 keV
   tracker hits: 8585 with 2.102 GeV of energy loss in the sensors, 0.245 MeV per hit (median 128 keV)
   Highland: a 1 GeV pion crossing 2.5 % X0 is deflected by 1.87 mrad (rms, one plane), a 10 GeV one by 0.185
   conversions: 313 (services 159, TEC 49, TOB 44, TID 21, TIB 19, PXB 9, beam pipe 7, PXF 5); bremsstrahlung photons above 10 MeV: 676
   of the 61 primary photons above 1 GeV in |eta| < 2.5, 40 converted in the tracker: 1 - exp(-7t/9) = 0.66 -> t = 1.37 X0 on average
   particles stopped in the tracker (kinetic energy below 10 MeV): 469

-- 4. hadronic physics
   nuclear interactions in the tracker: 163 (services 78, TEC 23, TOB 20, TIB 12, TID 10, beam pipe 10, PXB 7, PXF 3), 417 secondaries stored
   of the 93 charged hadrons with pT > 0.5 GeV in |eta| < 2.5, 32 (34 %) interact before the calorimeters: as if the tracker were 0.42 lambda_I thick
   hadrons whose shower starts in the crystals: 221, in the HCAL: 78, punch-through: 0
   a pion of     1 GeV: electromagnetic fraction 1 - (E/0.8)^(0.82 - 1) = 0.04; seen by the HCAL as 0.73 of an electron
   a pion of    10 GeV: electromagnetic fraction 1 - (E/0.8)^(0.82 - 1) = 0.37; seen by the HCAL as 0.82 of an electron
   a pion of   100 GeV: electromagnetic fraction 1 - (E/0.8)^(0.82 - 1) = 0.58; seen by the HCAL as 0.88 of an electron
   invisible energy of the hadronic showers: 158.3 GeV; in dead material between and behind the calorimeters: 124.3 GeV; beside every calorimeter (|eta| > 5.191): 819.1 GeV in 168 particles

